diff --git a/DOCS/edl-mpv.rst b/DOCS/edl-mpv.rst
--- a/DOCS/edl-mpv.rst
+++ b/DOCS/edl-mpv.rst
@@ -239,6 +239,11 @@
 If ``file.mkv`` has an audio and a video stream, both will use ``blabla`` as
 title. The subtitle stream will use ``ducks`` as title.
 
+The optional ``fps`` parameter supplies a finite advertised video frame rate
+for format menus. It is kept separately from the demuxer frame rate and does
+not change decoding or playback timing. Positive values take precedence in
+track and edition labels, including for streams opened immediately.
+
 The ``track_meta`` header is not part of the core EDL format. It may be changed
 or removed at any time, depending on mpv's internal requirements.
 
@@ -317,8 +322,8 @@
 ``fps``
     For video codecs: expected video framerate, as a finite floating-point
     number (for example, ``23.976`` or ``59.94``). Integer rates remain valid.
-    This is a hint for an unopened stream; opening it may refine the rate
-    using the actual media timestamps.
+    This supplies codec metadata for a delay-open stream. To keep format menus
+    independent of probing, also set ``fps`` in its ``track_meta`` header.
 
 ``samplerate``
     For audio codecs: expected sample rate, as integer.
diff --git a/DOCS/man/input.rst b/DOCS/man/input.rst
--- a/DOCS/man/input.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/input.rst
@@ -3606,6 +3606,11 @@
 
     ``track-list/N/demux-fps``
         Video FPS as indicated by the container. (Not always accurate.)
+
+    ``track-list/N/format-fps``
+        Advertised frame rate supplied by the format list, when available.
+        Track selectors prefer this stable value over ``demux-fps``. It does
+        not affect decoding or playback timing.
 
     ``track-list/N/demux-bitrate``
         Average bitrate, in bits per second. (Not always accurate.)
